Disclaimer: Axial psoriatic arthritis flares mimic structural back injuries but are driven by autoimmune inflammation; MRI may be required to confirm the extent of active sacroiliitis.
Clinical Course: The acute, locking spinal spasm will significantly diminish over 24-48 hours with continuous high-dose anti-inflammatory use.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Call 000 immediately if your legs suddenly give way, or if you lose the ability to control your bladder or bowels.

